        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Cover, linen embroidered with silk in surface darning on the diagonal over 3 threads and chain stitch (border).\nThe border consists of a green meandering stem with a small green leaf joining diagonal red flowers with a blue centre and a tulip in reserve; from the tip of the red flower and placed along the opposite diagonal is a blue leaf containing a red tulip. The field is decorated with blue parallel stems decorated internally by a red line with small white flowers (including pomegranates and tulips).  Alternating from the left and the right of these stems are large red leaves, each containing a green stem with blue and white flowers: a carnation, tulips and pomegranates. In addition a green and red tulip and a green leaf with a small red and white tulip grow from the large stems.\nThere is no embroidered border along the lower edge - just a green band. \nThree widths joined after being embroidered."@en ;
